    rdamd:P30137 "First edition; first printing, according to number line 9 to 1 on copyright page.\nKate Wilhelm is printed (as contributor) on the cover, but none of her work is included.\n'A Hunger Artist' translated by John Kessel.\n'The Lottery in Babylon' translated by Andrew Hurley.\nEach story is accompanied by 'Editors' Notes' at the end; all story introductions take the story's or the author's response to Kafka into account.\nExtended copyrights on p. 4; on p. 283 are Acknowledgments.\nCover artist credited on copyright page, but on back cover 'Brainchild Studios/NYC' is credited." ;
