man:643390
    a rdac:C10007 ;
    rdaxd:P00018 "http://entedit.org/manifestation/643390",
        "https://www.isfdb.org/cgi-bin/pl.cgi?643390" ;
    rdfs:label "Antæus, Spring/Summer 1977 (Ecco Press, 1977)" ;
    rdamd:P30156 "Antæus, Spring/Summer 1977"@en ;
    rdamd:P30117 "edited by Editors of Antæus" ;
    rdamd:P30176 "Ecco Press" ;
    rdamd:P30011 "1977-04" ;
    rdamd:P30182 "336 p." ;
    rdamd:P30004 "LCCN 70-612646" ;
    rdamd:P30137 "#25/26\nGenerally a literary journal, Antæus occasionally had special issues devoted to fiction. This issue is one of those, and is the only one with a substantial amount of science fiction. This issue was divided equally between Western, Detective, and Science Fiction genres. (The cover is from the Detective section, and hence is not included here.)\nPartial contents only, limited to the science fiction genre stories, on pp. 218-336.\nBack cover is an ad for Raymond Chandler's books The Notebooks of Raymond Chandler and English Summer: A Gothic Romance with a photo of the author.\nPrice printed on p. 2: \"Single copies $3.50 (£2.00 U.K.)\"\nArtist credit on p. 5." ;
    rdamo:P30001 rdact:1049 ;
    rdamo:P30002 rdamt:1007 ;
    rdamo:P30420 pbl:605 ;
    rdamo:P30363 per:262892 ;
    entedit:P03 per:820 ;
