    rdamd:P30182 "xliv+598 p." ;
    rdamd:P30004 "ISBN 9780575108028" ;
    rdamd:P30106 "Gollancz SF Masterworks (II)" ;
    rdamd:P30137 "Stated 4th printing of the 2012 edition, by number line.\nTitle page:\nGollancz colophon as imprint.\nCopyright page:\n\"Introduction copyright © Adam Roberts 2011\"\n\"Introduction Year 2002 by Harlan Ellison. [over] Copyright © The Kilimanjaro Corporation 2002\"\n\"Foreword Year 2002 by Michael Moorcock. [over] Copyright © The Kilimanjaro Corporation 2002\"\n\"Dangerous Visions® edited by Harlan Ellison. [over] Copyright © Harlan Ellison 1967 [over] Renewed, 1995 by The Kilimanjaro Corporation.\"\n\"Dangerous Visions® 35th Anniversary Edition. [over] Copyright © The Kilimanjaro Corporation 2002\"\n\"Illustrations by Leo & Diane Dillon. [over] Copyright © Leo & Diane Dillon 1967 [over] Renewed, 1995 by Leo & Diane Dillon.\"\n\"This edition published in Great Britain in 2012 by Gollancz [over] An imprint of the Orion Publishing Group [over] An Hachette UK Company\"\nNumber line \"5 7 9 10 8 6 4\"\nTable of Contents errors, page vii:\nAsimov's Foreword 1 - given as page xxiii.\nAsimov's Foreword 2 - given as page xxx.\nEllison's 1967: Introduction Thirty-Two Soothsayers - given as page xxxiv; Harlan spelt correctly.\nPage numbers given in ToC are for Ellison's story introductions.\nBack cover:\n\"UK £9.99\" (no additional pricing)\n\"Illustration by Vincent Chong\" (no visible signature on the artwork)\nEvery introduction is headed with a b&w illustration by Leo & Diane Dillon.\nAcknowledgements are on page xliv: \"Harlan Ellison [over] Hollywood [over] 14 February 1967\".\nThe essay 'Introduction to Evensong:' by Harlan Ellison starts on unnumbered page 1.\nSemi-gloss cover.\nAll data from UK library copy." ;
